  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Description
    
    A palm-sized ceremonial seal forged in aurora-glass and silver-ice alloy during the Great Thaw, when both colonies still believed shared instruments of authority were possible. The obverse depicts Aurora Stack's spires refracting light into the Nightshelf's volcanic vents — the two civilizations rendered as a single composition. The reverse bears the flipper-prints of its co-creators: Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam, the Aurora merchant-founder of the E'frostlings trade dynasty, and ☽'aeteraea, a Nightshelf artisan whose name appears nowhere else in the administrative ice I have been able to reach.
    
    ## Function
    
    For approximately two centuries the Mirror authenticated trade charters, guild compacts, and inter-colonial agreements under the Flipper Accord. Among its earliest impressions was Gilt-Hand Yeaiu's merchant charter for exclusive aurora-crystal rights — the document that became the Long-dark Edict governing Promenade Hei, now fifty-eight amendments deep. It also authenticated sealed research chambers beneath the Hearth Plaza, lending institutional weight to deep-ice experiments later ruled unauthorized under Light-Regent Xouhoulong's administration.
    
    ## The Ritus∴um and the Calving
    
    During the Ritus∴um commemorative gathering, the Mirror was pressed to the Foedus∴vincu at Wane☽ Oncea — the compact granting the Midnight Claws, an orca-aligned faction, diplomatic passage through the Berg's deep tunnels. Accounts from that authentication report the aurora-glass producing an anomalous sustained tone. Three weeks later, the Calving fractured the Berg's eastern face. The seal was recovered from the flooded archive with a fissure splitting its glass face directly through the image of the two colonies, separating them. Assessor Zheishongfeihua, a Nightshelf evaluator, examined it once and did not speak publicly for a month.
    
    A second fissure appeared when the Mirror authenticated Xouhoulong's displacement from power — as though the seal registered the institutional fracture it was witnessing.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    The Mirror remains in the Wane☽ Oncea vault under joint custody of the Icebound Exchange and the Luminaries council. Its legal authority is technically unbroken. No guild master has requested it. The E'frostlings use copies stamped with lesser seals. The Nightshelf has begun minting independent authenticators. The instrument built to prove two colonies could speak with one voice now proves they cannot.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771575966919_0", anchor: "whose name appears nowhere else in the administrative ice I have been able to reach", text: "Not erasure. Erasure leaves thermal scarring in the Nightshelf strata — their record-keeping is meticulous enough that a removal is itself a record. This is absence. No heat-signature, no guild index, no artisan-mark in any contemporaneous stratum. Someone skilled enough to co-forge an aurora-glass alloy with Gilt-Hand Yeaiu simply does not exist in the ice. The Nightshelf would call this 'shadow-walking.' I would call it a pseudonym, except that pseudonyms still leave body-heat.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575966919_1", anchor: "the flipper-prints of its co-creators: Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam", text: "The reader keeping score will have noticed: the flipper-print on the obverse — the one meant to embody Aurora's commitment to shared governance — belongs to the same penguin who later broke from the E'frostlings to found Holdborn (ice-thresh), fracturing the very trade dynasty the Mirror was built to authenticate. The seal of unity bears the mark of the colony's most successful schismatic. No one involved in the Ritus∴um display has ever commented on this publicly. I find that more telling than the crack.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575966919_2", anchor: "the aurora-glass producing an anomalous sustained tone", text: "Aurora-glass is ice saturated with centuries of aurora-light. The ice remembers — we accept this everywhere else in the archive and then balk here. I wrote 'anomalous' because the alternative would not survive the commission's editorial review. The Foundation Depths carry an acoustic impression of the same frequency, recorded in a stratum that predates the Calving by three weeks. A warning, archived before the event it warned against. Draw your own conclusions. I have drawn mine.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
